    "a": "Claims must match what the product is registered or filed to say, and the evidence summary behind them has to be published. Medical wording, absolute terms, guarantees of efficacy and efficacy implied through an ingredient's function are all banned. Whitening, spot removal, sun protection and hair-loss claims require registration as special cosmetics first."
  },
  {
    "q": "Do skincare efficacy claims need testing in China?",
    "a": "Some do. China's efficacy evaluation standard requires a human efficacy test for six claims: spot removal and whitening, sun protection, hair-loss prevention, acne, nourishing and repair. Other claims can rest on evaluation tests, literature or research data analysis. Sensory claims like cleansing and fragrance, and purely physical effects, are exempt from publishing a summary."
  },
  {
    "q": "Can beauty ads in China show before and after images?",
    "a": "No national cosmetics instrument bans them outright. Fabricating a use effect is false advertising under the Advertising Law, Shanghai's local guideline bars fabricated or edited before-and-after footage while allowing moderate artistic rendering, and a regional regulator fined two sellers over before-and-after images in February 2025. Treat the Shanghai language as the working standard."
  },
  {
    "q": "What does a beauty brand need for Tmall, Douyin and RedNote?",
    "a": "A main image set with a white-background image, a long detail page, a separate mobile detail page, a spec chart, store banners and short video, plus vertical video at 9:16 for Douyin and a 3:4 cover for RedNote. The parts are stable across every source checked. The pixel values are counted from published sources, not read from the platforms, so confirm them in your own backend."
  },
  {
    "q": "Can retouching or AI skin break Chinese platform rules?",
    "a": "Yes. One marketplace's AI fake-image rule names distorted or exaggerated product effects as a failure category and enforces it with a detection model at upload. Shanghai's guideline separately bars misleading consumers through excessive retouching. Generated content also carries visible and metadata labeling duties under rules in force since September 2025."
  }
